# A globally reserved structural word (spec/grammar.md#keywords-primitives-and-built-in-names) heads no alternative of the
# `expression` production (spec/grammar.md#expressions-and-calls), so the reader reports each as ol-bad-token at
# the offending token — "a valid OpenLogo token ... not permitted at the current grammar position"
# (spec/error-model.md#normative-code-registry). Before issue #853 all six below parsed AND checked completely CLEAN
# under every profile set: nothing said so.
#
# The first two lines are the issue's verbatim reproduction. The rest use a list element — a full
# `expression` by spec/grammar.md#expressions-and-calls — because the Data mutation heads (spec/grammar.md#ebnf-notation)
# are ALSO statement openers, so at the start of a statement the reader's error recovery re-enters
# their statement form and adds a second, incidental diagnostic. Pinning them in a non-statement
# value position keeps this stack-neutral contract about ACCEPTANCE, not about one reader's
# recovery strategy. Parse-only negative fixture.
repeat value [ ]
repeat key [ ]
:first = [ add ]
:second = [ remove ]
:third = [ insert ]
:fourth = [ clear ]
